Because each new level takes geometrically more points from
killing monsters, this has different context as you go.

For a character who wants to advance rather than avoid
advancing, I like to stay on level 1 until I am XP=2 and may
end up at XP=3 in rare instances before descending to fully
explore level 2.  I am usually XP=3 before I descend to fully
explore level 3.  This pattern stops working very quickly in
the main dungeon, though.  Especially if I do the monster
rich mines before Sokoban.

By the time the character has finished the minesand Sokoban
being able to advance another level with combat starts to
take so much extra time it gets ridiculous to expect to advance
before descending.  It's only a strategy for the first few levels
of the game.



